                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I would not recommend this game what-so-ever. The controls aren't too clunky and the platfoming can be fun at times but Habitus suffers from a major fundamental issue. It's boring. Like really boring. Watching paint dry would be more exciting than playing this poor excuse of a game labeling itself as \"entertainment\". You run around a randomly generated level looking for sources of food to bring back to your camp so you can end the level and do it all over again. It's repetitive and dull. Like I said, the platforming can be fun at times but that is all this game has going for it. The enemies are more annoying than threatening and the random level generator doesn't seem to be optimized too well, as levels often have long narrow tunnels leading no where.  It's tagged as \"survival\" but I think that's a bit far-fetched. Yes, the whole premise is about being a cave man and trying to find food to survive, but the food in the game might as well be a score because it's only purpose is to be an arbitrary goal for the level. Their is nothing to the food counter other than that. Habitus is as much of a survival game as super mario brothers is. Nothing new is going on in this game, it's a drag to play through and the developer is asking for way too much. I wouldn't pay fifty cents fo this game let alone three dollars. Just skip it, you will be doing yourself a favor.",
